<h1>Curriculum Overview</h1>

<h2>What is AI and the Systems that Power It about?</h2>

<p>This unit explores how AI and computing systems process information and interact with hardware and software, through hands-on design, troubleshooting, and ethical evaluation of AI's real-world impact.</p>

<div style="background-color:#F7F7FB; border-left:4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius:8px; padding:12px 16px; margin:20px 0;">
<div style="font-size:16px;">
<p>This is the second unit in the six unit <a href="https://studio.code.org/courses/artificial-intelligence-foundations-2026/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><b>AI Foundations</b></a> semester 1 course. This professional learning module prepares you to teach it!</p>
</div>
</div>

<h2>Student Learning Goals</h2>

<div style="background-color:#F7F7FB; border-left:4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius:8px; padding:12px 16px; margin:20px 0;">
<div style="font-size:16px;">
<p><b>Students will:</b></p>
<p>• Explain how AI and computing systems process information and interact with hardware and software.</p>
<p>• Design, troubleshoot, and optimize computing systems while exploring emerging technologies like IoT and robotics.</p>
<p>• Apply human-centered design principles to develop AI-driven solutions for real-world problems.</p>
<p>• Critically evaluate AI-generated outputs for accuracy, reliability, and potential biases.</p>
</div>
</div>

<h2>Unit Length and Format</h2>

<p><b>Total Duration:</b> Approximately 3 weeks<br>
<b>Structure:</b> Twelve 45-minute lessons and one 3-day culminating project</p>

<h3>Unit Calendar</h3>

<p>Take a quick look at the lessons included in this unit using the calendar tool. This version of the calendar assumes 5 45-minute lessons per week.</p>

